# ── gen491 (2026-09-01) — PERCHE' LE ATTESE «Learned: pred(arg)» SONO CAMBIATE ─
#
# Questo file asseriva la NOTAZIONE come risposta attesa: «Learned: man(socrates).»
# Un ratchet che congela un difetto lo difende con l'autorita' di un verde, ed
# era il caso: la risposta principale di parrot0 non era LINGUA, e l'audit
# dell'eco (scripts/self_echo_audit.py) ha mostrato che rileggendosi parrot0
# chiamava la propria notazione «a snippet of code» — non la riconosceva come
# propria.
#
# Le attese sono state ritirate, non allineate a un comportamento qualunque: la
# sostituzione e' avvenuta SOLO dove il vecchio atteso era un termine e il nuovo
# e' la frase corrispondente. L'invariante che regge il cambio sta in
# tests/p0t/conversation/self_echo.p0t — tutto cio' che parrot0 dice deve
# essergli comprensibile — e adesso la conferma e' un punto fisso:
#
#     > a whale is a mammal      →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#     > whale is a mammal        →  Learned: whale is a mammal.
#
# migrated from tests/cases/emerge.chat (gen346, hermetic + isolated)
[mock hermetic]
!set PARROT0_BASE=
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test emerge]
# gen79: emergent rule induction. After each RULE assertion, kb_induce runs
# and any newly discovered implications are announced as "Induced: ...".
# The induction is statistical: implications hold where ALL known entities
# of one class are also in another (minimum 2 support).
# Setup: 3 dogs, 2 pets. Lassie is a dog but not a pet.
> rex is a dog
< Learned: rex is a dog.
> fido is a dog
< Learned: fido is a dog.
> lassie is a dog
< Learned: lassie is a dog.
> rex is a pet
< Learned: rex is a pet.
> fido is a pet
< Learned: fido is a pet.
# Rule: every pet is a dog (true). No new inductions because
# the reverse (dog→pet) is false (lassie is a dog but not a pet).
> every pet is a dog
< Learned rule: dog(X) :- pet(X).
# Add a third category shared by rex and fido but NOT lassie.
> rex is a happy
< Learned: rex is a happy.
> fido is a happy
< Learned: fido is a happy.
# Rule: every pet is happy. Since all pets = rex, fido = all happy,
# induction finds bidirectional implications with happy.
> every pet is a happy
< Learned rule: happy(X) :- pet(X). Induced: dog(X) :- happy(X). pet(X) :- happy(X).

